    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-040 Commit 1 of 2** — parse-time expansion of `border: <width> <style> <color>` and per-side forms. **Pure CSS parse path** — zero layout.cpp or paint.cpp changes.\n\nCloses the gap surfaced by ADR-039: `border: 1px solid X` was producing no visible border because ADR-012 expands `border-width` but not the 3-token `border` shorthand.\n\n⚠️ **DO NOT MERGE until PNG verification passes.** ADR-039 was reverted precisely because it shipped mixed-risk without PNG inspection. ADR-040's Verification section codifies \"render and inspect PNG before merge.\" The merge button stays untouched until the before/after PNGs are confirmed.\n\n## What changed\n\n### `src/renderer/css/stylesheet.cpp` (+123 lines)\n\n**New helpers:**\n\n- `is_border_width_token(s)` — accepts `0`, `thin`, `medium`, `thick`, or any token starting with `[0-9.]`\n- `is_border_style_keyword(s)` — CSS border-style set (`none`, `hidden`, `solid`, `dashed`, `dotted`, `double`, `groove`, `ridge`, `inset`, `outset`)\n- `struct BorderTriple { width, style, color, has_color }` + `parse_border_tokens(tokens, out)` — classifies 1/2/3-token forms\n- `try_expand_border(value, important, out)` — emits `border-width` / `border-style` / `border-color`\n- `try_expand_border_side(property, value, important, out)` — emits `border-{side}-{width,style,color}`\n\n**Dispatcher** in `expand_shorthand()` — `border` and per-side branches after `flex-flow`, before `is_box_shorthand`. Malformed forms drop the declaration (matching `grid-template` / `flex` / `flex-flow` behavior).\n\n### `tests/test_stylesheet.cpp` (+142/−1 lines)\n\n**10 new tests** tagged `[css][stylesheet][adr-040]`:\n\n| Test | What it verifies |\n|---|---|\n| `border: 1px solid #ccc` | 3 longhands, correct values |\n| `border: 0` | `border-width: 0` only |\n| `border: none` | `border-width: 0` only |\n| `border: 5px none red` | `border-width: 0` (CSS spec §8.5.3) |\n| `border: 1px dashed red` | style preserved verbatim (paint defers dashes) |\n| `border: 1px solid red !important` | `!important` preserved |\n| `border-top: 2px solid blue` | 3 per-side longhands |\n| `border-left: 0` | `border-left-width: 0` only |\n| `border: foo bar baz` | rule dropped |\n| `border-width: 5px` | ADR-012 regression — still expands to 4 longhands |\n\n**1 test decoupled**: `\"var(): embedded var() in composite value resolved (ADR-037)\"` used `border: 1px solid var(...)` as its composite-value vehicle, asserting `declarations.size() == 1`. Post-ADR-040 that assertion fails (3 longhands). Changed vehicle to `outline:` — same composite shape, same var() intent, still 1 declaration. Comment in the test documents the decoupling.\n\n## Verification\n\n### Unit tests (this PR — commit 1)\n\n- **504 / 504 cases pass**, 1927 assertions\n- Zero warnings, zero failures\n- `git diff --name-only` confirms only `stylesheet.cpp` + `test_stylesheet.cpp` touched\n\n### PNG verification (required before merge)\n\n**Nothing merges until the before/after PNGs are confirmed.** Run:\n\n    ./build/bin/honeybee\n\nThen in the browser:\n\n1. Type `https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTML`, Enter, wait for full load\n2. **BEFORE**: check out `main` at `9792124`, build, run, capture first-viewport PNG\n3. **AFTER**: check out `feat/border-shorthand` at `ee21a0e`, build, run, capture first-viewport PNG\n4. Compare — the 2 expected diffs:\n\n| Element | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `form.cdx-search-input` | No border | **1px gray border** |\n| `h1#firstHeading` | No underline | **1px gray bottom underline** |\n\n5. **Also check for unintended borders** — body, header background, article container, navboxes, sidebars. If ANY unintended border appears, the PR stays open for a fix. The `border: 1px solid transparent` cases (`.vector-column-start`, `.vector-column-end`) should produce NO visual change.\n\n**Merge criteria:** both expected borders appear, zero unintended borders.\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before this PR: **494 cases / 1881 assertions**\n- After this PR: **504 cases / 1927 assertions** (+10 cases, +46 assertions)\n\n## Deliberately out of scope (per ADR-040)\n\n- `border-style: dashed | dotted` — paint-side change, 0 uses in Wikipedia\n- `border-radius` — needs Cairo arc support, own ADR\n- `border-collapse` / `border-spacing` — table category\n- `border: <width> <color>` 2-token — documented CSS-spec deviation, 0 uses in target\n- `parent_content_height` → ADR-041\n- `overflow: auto | scroll` → ADR-042\n\n## What's next (Commit 2 of 2, after merge)\n\nDocs commit:\n- ADR-040 status → Implemented\n- Measured visible delta recorded (actual PNG diff, not predicted)\n- Post-ADR-040 note in ADR-012\n- README row update\n- CHANGELOG entry\n\n**Refs #204**\n",
